<article>
    <h1>{$selectedSection}</h1>
    <p>We'll assume that the reader is familiar with basic meaning of position, time, speed, acceleration etc. In this chapter, these basic notions will be presented in more detail. Description of motion of an object requires specifying observer and time, i.e. the <em>frame of reference</em>.</p>
    <section>
        <h2>Frame of reference</h2>
        <p>
            A frame of reference is a co-ordinate system like we introduced in <a href="/iitphysics/Physics%20and%20Mathematics/Resolution%20of%20Vectors">Resolution of Vectors</a>. In addition to co-ordinate system, a frame of reference has a clock to measure time. Measurement of position, velocity and accelerations are done with respect to the chosen frame of reference.
        </p>
